To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Freedom of Information Act, I hereby request the following records:

Pursuant to the Freedom of Information Act, I request all records maintained by the Executive Office for United States Attorneys (EOUSA), including records held by or associated with the United States Attorney’s Offices for the Southern District of New York, Middle District of Pennsylvania and United States attorneys office for the eastern district of Minnesota, concerning Christopher Furnari’s federal parole proceedings.

Furnari Bureau of Prisons Register Number is 
19815-054

This request specifically includes the entirety of the approximately two-foot stack of files referenced in a United States Parole Commission Original Jurisdiction Appeal Summary concerning Furnari, Reg. No. 19815-054. I will attach a copy of this document.

If the approximately two-foot collection is maintained under a case number, matter number, file number, subject number, box number, archive identifier, or other internal identifier, please provide that identifier and any associated index, inventory, file-control record, routing sheet, transfer record, or other record sufficient to identify the complete collection.

Scope of the Requested Parole Records

I request the complete body of records concerning Furnari’s federal parole, including records concerning his parole eligibility, parole hearings, reconsideration proceedings, appeals, requests for reconsideration, release considerations, government recommendations or objections, and any other federal parole proceeding involving Furnari.

This includes all records pertaining to the following but is not limited to:

* records submitted to, received from, or exchanged with the United States Parole Commission;
* records concerning the Government’s position regarding Furnari’s release;
* recommendations, objections, memoranda, letters, reports, factual submissions, and other materials submitted in support of or opposition to parole;
* records concerning the offense-severity category assigned to Furnari and the factual basis used to support that determination;
* records concerning his guideline calculations, salient factor score, aggravating circumstances, or other factors considered in determining whether he should be released;
* records concerning information used to deny, defer, oppose, or otherwise adversely affect Furnari’s parole;
* records concerning any subsequent reconsideration or review of those decisions;
* internal memoranda, correspondence, notes, emails, and other communications concerning how the United States Attorney’s Office responded to Furnari’s parole proceedings;
* communications between EOUSA, the relevant United States Attorney’s Offices, the Bureau of Prisons, the United States Parole Commission, federal courts, and other federal or state agencies concerning Furnari’s parole; and
* records concerning any federal litigation arising from or relating to Furnari’s parole.

records concerning the murders, attempted murders, or other criminal conduct attributed to Furnari in connection with his parole proceedings, including information concerning Lee Schleifer, Richard Taglianetti, Frank DeCicco, Joseph Abinanti, Anthony Luongo, and any other offense or incident relied upon by the government in seeking to establish a Severity of Offense Behavior Category Eight classification.

Underlying Evidence and Investigative Material Used in Furnari’s Parole Proceedings

This request also includes underlying investigative, prosecutorial, evidentiary, witness, informant, or other records to the extent that those records were used, obtained, reviewed, relied upon, summarized, incorporated, transmitted, or otherwise brought into Furnari’s federal parole proceedings or parole-related litigation.

I am aware that records concerning individuals such as Anthony Casso, Alphonse D’Arco, Thomas Carew, and others appear throughout federal litigation and other records relating to Furnari.

I am therefore specifically requesting records concerning such individuals where their statements, debriefings, testimony, reports, information, or other materials were used in connection with Furnari’s federal parole proceedings or litigation concerning those proceedings.

The publicly available federal judicial opinions establish that the government relied upon witness information from Casso, D’Arco, and Carew, and that Furnari specifically challenged the government’s reliance upon that information and sought the underlying FBI 302s. These matters were litigated extensively in federal court over a period of many years.

Federal courts have already extensively described and litigated the government’s reliance upon information from Anthony Casso, Alphonse D’Arco, and Thomas Carew in Furnari’s parole proceedings. See, among other authorities, Furnari v. Warden, Allenwood Federal Correctional Institution, 218 F.3d 250 (3d Cir. 2000), and Furnari v. United States Parole Commission, 531 F.3d 241 (3d Cir. 2008). I am also requesting all records which are referred to by the government or Furnari in all federal litigation involving Furnari’s parole matters. I have provided some authorities above but it is not an exhaustive list

I therefore request that EOUSA not withhold records merely because they contain information concerning witnesses or informants where the same information, witness identity, testimony, interview material, or substantive allegations have already been publicly disclosed through federal litigation.


This includes, without limitation:

* witness debriefings;
* FBI or other investigative reports;
* interview reports and memoranda;
* statements or summaries attributed to Casso, D’Arco, Carew, or other witnesses or cooperating individuals;
* information concerning alleged murders, attempted murders, organized-crime activity, or other conduct attributed to Furnari;
* records used to establish or support the severity of Furnari’s offense for parole purposes;
* records cited or relied upon in Government submissions opposing or affecting Furnari’s release;
* records provided to the Parole Commission;
* records used in preparing Government responses to Furnari’s parole applications or appeals;
* and records used in federal litigation concerning the legality or factual basis of a Parole Commission decision concerning Furnari.

The fact that a record concerns an investigation or another individual does not make it outside the scope of this request where that record was subsequently used or maintained in connection with Furnari’s federal parole.

I am not requesting unrelated investigative files concerning Casso, D’Arco, Carew, or other individuals merely because they mention Furnari. The requested material is limited to records having a substantive connection to Furnari’s federal parole proceedings or litigation arising from those proceedings.

Where matters pertaining to Furnari’s parole refers to information originating from Casso, D’Arco, Carew, or other witnesses/cooperating individuals, please include the underlying records maintained by EOUSA or the relevant United States Attorney’s Office to the extent those records were used or relied upon in that litigation.

Records Supporting Parole Denials or Continued Incarceration

I specifically request records reflecting the factual or evidentiary basis for any Government position that Furnari should not be released on parole, should remain incarcerated, should receive a later reconsideration date, or should otherwise be denied or delayed in obtaining release.

This includes records identifying or discussing:

* reasons for opposing release;
* aggravating factors;
* alleged conduct considered relevant to parole;
* information concerning Furnari’s role in organized crime;
* information concerning murders or other violent conduct attributed to Furnari;
* information concerning his offense severity;
* information concerning his conduct while incarcerated, where considered in parole proceedings;
* information concerning prior or subsequent criminal conduct, where considered for parole purposes;
* witness or informant information relied upon against Furnari;
* and any other information used to argue that Furnari should remain incarcerated.

Complete Parole-Related File and Cross-References

Please search for both main-file and cross-reference records relating to Furnari’s federal parole.

Where a parole-related record references another file, investigation, prosecution, witness, document, exhibit, memorandum, or other source that was used in connection with Furnari’s parole, please search for and provide that underlying record to the extent it is maintained by EOUSA or a United States Attorney’s Office and falls within the scope of this request.

The request therefore includes records that may not themselves be titled or indexed as “parole” records but which were incorporated into, relied upon for, or maintained in connection with Furnari’s parole proceedings.

he publicly available judicial record demonstrates that Furnari’s parole proceedings involved substantial factual and evidentiary material concerning alleged murders, violent conduct, organized-crime activity, and information attributed to witnesses and cooperating individuals, including Anthony Casso and Alfonso D’Arco.

For example, the Third Circuit’s published decisions describe the Government’s production of evidence concerning Furnari’s alleged involvement in murders and other violent acts during his initial parole proceedings, the Commission’s Category Eight determination, its reliance upon information attributed to Casso, and later consideration of information attributed to D’Arco. 

Accordingly, please treat references in judicial opinions, pleadings, exhibits, Government filings, Parole Commission records, and other publicly available materials to particular evidence, witnesses, investigations, reports, or factual allegations as search leads for the underlying EOUSA records, rather than limiting the search to documents whose titles contain the word “parole.”

In particular, where a Government filing, court submission, Parole Commission submission, memorandum, or other record identifies or relies upon a particular investigative report, witness statement, debriefing, interview, memorandum, FBI report, prosecution file, or other source, please search for the underlying record and any EOUSA/USAO copy, referral, transmittal, summary, or derivative document maintained by the Government.

Records Systems and Archived Holdings

Please conduct a comprehensive search of the EOUSA records and information systems reasonably expected to contain responsive material, including current, legacy, retired, archived, physical, electronic, and off-site records.

This includes, but is not limited to,
   •    The USA-5 case management system, LIONS, and any retired or legacy databases;
   •    The Criminal, Civil, Asset Forfeiture, and Appeals divisions’ electronic and paper files;
   •    The Records Information Management System (RIMS) and any archived boxes or transferred holdings;

* USA-001 – Administrative File System
* USA-003 – Citizen Complaint Files
* USA-005 – Civil Case Files
* USA-006 – Consumer Complaint Files
* USA-007 – Criminal Case Files
* USA-009 – Kline District of Columbia and Maryland Stock and Land Fraud Inter-Relationship Filing System
* USA-010 – Major Crimes Division Investigative Files
* USA-011 – Prosecutor’s Management Information System (PROMIS)
* USA-013 – U.S. Attorney, District of Columbia Superior Court Division, Criminal Files
* USA-014 – Pre-Trial Diversion Program Files

Please cross-reference searches between these systems and the records of the Southern District of New York and Middle District of Pennsylvania, as well as any other United States Attorney’s Office or EOUSA component reasonably likely to possess responsive records.

The search should include Federal Records Center holdings, archived and retired files, and any other location where historical EOUSA or United States Attorney’s Office records may reasonably be maintained.

Records No Longer Maintained

If the approximately two-foot file, or any other responsive Furnari parole records, are no longer maintained by EOUSA or the relevant United States Attorney’s Office, please provide records sufficient to establish their disposition, including any transfer, accession, archival, retirement, or destruction records.

If responsive material was transferred to another DOJ component, Federal Records Center, NARA, or another repository, please identify the receiving location and any available accession, box, file, transfer, or other identifying information.

Segregability and Withholdings

If any responsive record is withheld in whole or in part, please release all reasonably segregable portions and identify the specific exemption relied upon for each withholding or redaction.

For records withheld in full, please provide an itemized description of the withheld material, including the number of pages or other records withheld, to the extent permitted by law.

I’ve included proof of Furnari’s status as deceased (obituary) Including the document which proves the existence of the stack of files for this case which take up approximately two feet of space

I am reserving my right for a fee waiver at the moment

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 20 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

L. Joe
